            <ArticleTitle>Chronic left main coronary artery occlusion: a complication of radiofrequency ablation of idiopathic left ventricular tachycardia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1874-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe in this report the development of chronic left main coronary artery (LMCA) occlusion in a young patient 2 years after an uncomplicated, successful ablation of idiopathic left ventricular tachycardia. This complication appears to be a late consequence of trauma to the LMCA during the procedure rather than an acute or subacute embolic event.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
